module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.AlgebraSheafImageQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FiniteTypeChartSections

/-!
# The subalgebra of an algebra on an algebraic space generated by two subalgebras

Let `F` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B`, and let
`c : C ⟶ A` and `d : D ⟶ A` be morphisms of sheaves of `𝒪_F`-algebras on the small étale site
of `F`.  Over an étale chart `V` the products `c(x) * d(x')` of a section of `C` and a section
of `D` span, as an `𝒪_F(V)`-module, the subring of `A(V)` generated by the images of `C(V)` and
of `D(V)`.  This file proves that membership in that span **descends** along a finite jointly
faithfully flat family of affine étale charts.

This is the generation statement that the existence of upper bounds in Stacks 082B needs: the
subalgebra of `A` generated by two subalgebras is, over an affine chart, generated by the
products of sections of the two, and the obstruction to seeing this is that a section of the
generated subalgebra over an affine chart is only *locally* a combination of such products.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.sectionsModule`: the sections of an algebra sheaf over
  an étale chart, as a module over the chart ring; it is the module of sections of the
  underlying `𝒪_F`-module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.sectionsMulBilin`: multiplication of the sections over
  a chart, as a bilinear map for that module structure.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.productSet`: the set of products of a section of `C` and
  a section of `D` over a chart, pushed into `A`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.productSet_restrict_subset_span`: for a morphism of
  affine étale charts `V ⟶ W`, every product of sections over `V` lies in the span of the
  restrictions of the products of sections over `W`, provided `C` and `D` are cartesian on
  affine charts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.mem_span_productSet_of_forall_restrict`: **a section
  over an affine étale chart lies in the span of the products as soon as its restriction to
  each member of a finite jointly faithfully flat family of affine charts does.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.span_productSet_eq_closure`: the span of the products is
  the subring of `A(V)` generated by the images of `C(V)` and of `D(V)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.mem_span_productSet_of_forall_restrict_of_isQuasicoherent`:
  the descent statement under quasi-coherence of the three algebras.

## Implementation notes

The scalar action of the chart ring on the sections of an algebra sheaf is multiplication
through the structure-algebra map, so multiplication of sections is `𝒪_F(V)`-bilinear and
`Submodule.map₂` turns a product of spans into the span of the pointwise products.  This is
what replaces a double induction in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.productSet_restrict_subset_span` and in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.mul_mem_span_productSet`.

The descent itself is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_of_forall_restrict_mem_span`, which asks
for a *single* finite family of sections over the large chart that works for every member of the
covering family.  The finite families produced member by member are amalgamated by indexing over
the sigma type of the chosen finite subsets, which is finite.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 082B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/082B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F)

variable {B S hS F hF}

/-! ### Sections of a module over a smaller chart as a span of restrictions -/

/-- Where the base change comparison along a morphism of charts is surjective, every section
over the smaller chart lies in the `𝒪_F(V)`-span of the restrictions of the sections over the
larger one. -/
theorem mem_span_range_chartRestrict (G : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    {W V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (g : V ⟶ W)
    (hG : Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange G g)) (x : G.val.obj (op V)) :
    x ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      (Set.range fun t : G.val.obj (op W) => chartRestrictLinear G g t) := by
  rw [show Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      (Set.range fun t : G.val.obj (op W) => chartRestrictLinear G g t) = ⊤ from
    (chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top G g).mp hG]
  exact Submodule.mem_top

namespace AlgebraSheaf

/-! ### The sections of an algebra sheaf over a chart as a module over the chart ring -/

/-- The sections of an algebra sheaf over an étale chart, as a module over the chart ring: the
scalar action is multiplication through the structure-algebra map, so this is the module of
sections of the underlying `𝒪_F`-module. -/
instance sectionsModule (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF) (V : SmallEtale B S hS F) :
    Module (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (A.right.obj.obj (op V)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (A.underlyingModule.val.obj (op V)))

/-- Scalars act on the sections of an algebra sheaf by multiplication through the
structure-algebra map. -/
theorem smul_sections (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF) (V : SmallEtale B S hS F)
    (r : chartRing B S hS F hF V) (x : A.right.obj.obj (op V)) :
    r • x = A.algebraMap (op V) r * x :=
  rfl

/-- Restriction of the sections of the module underlying an algebra sheaf is restriction of the
sections of the sheaf of rings. -/
theorem chartRestrictLinear_underlyingModule (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    {W V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (g : V ⟶ W) (y : A.right.obj.obj (op W)) :
    chartRestrictLinear A.underlyingModule g y = A.right.obj.map g.op y :=
  rfl

/-- Multiplication of the sections of an algebra sheaf over an étale chart, as an
`𝒪_F(V)`-bilinear map: scalars act by multiplication through the structure-algebra map, and the
sections form a commutative ring. -/
def sectionsMulBilin (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF) (V : SmallEtale B S hS F) :
    A.right.obj.obj (op V) →ₗ[chartRing B S hS F hF V]
      A.right.obj.obj (op V) →ₗ[chartRing B S hS F hF V] A.right.obj.obj (op V) :=
  LinearMap.mk₂ (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (fun y z => y * z)
    (fun y₁ y₂ z => add_mul y₁ y₂ z)
    (fun r y z => mul_assoc (A.algebraMap (op V) r) y z)
    (fun y z₁ z₂ => mul_add y z₁ z₂)
    (fun r y z => mul_left_comm y (A.algebraMap (op V) r) z)

/-- The bilinear multiplication `sectionsMulBilin A V` sends `y` and `z` to their product
`y * z`. -/
@[simp]
theorem sectionsMulBilin_apply (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF) (V : SmallEtale B S hS F)
    (y z : A.right.obj.obj (op V)) : sectionsMulBilin A V y z = y * z :=
  rfl

/-! ### The products of sections of two algebras over a chart -/

/-- The set of products of a section of `C` and a section of `D` over an étale chart, pushed
into `A` along `c` and `d`.  Its `𝒪_F(V)`-span is the subring of `A(V)` generated by the images
of `C(V)` and of `D(V)`. -/
def productSet {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A)
    (V : SmallEtale B S hS F) : Set (A.right.obj.obj (op V)) :=
  {y | ∃ (x : C.right.obj.obj (op V)) (x' : D.right.obj.obj (op V)),
    y = c.right.hom.app (op V) x * d.right.hom.app (op V) x'}

/-- A product of elements of two spans lies in a span as soon as all products of the generators
do. -/
private theorem mul_mem_span_of_forall_mul_mem
    {A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} {V : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    {s t u : Set (A.right.obj.obj (op V))} {y₁ y₂ : A.right.obj.obj (op V)}
    (h₁ : y₁ ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) s)
    (h₂ : y₂ ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) t)
    (h : ∀ p ∈ s, ∀ q ∈ t, p * q ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) u) :
    y₁ * y₂ ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) u := by
  have h' := Submodule.apply_mem_map₂ (sectionsMulBilin A V) h₁ h₂
  rw [Submodule.map₂_span_span] at h'
  refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_ h'
  rintro v ⟨p, hp, q, hq, rfl⟩
  exact h p hp q hq

/-- The `𝒪_F(V)`-span of the products of sections of `C` and `D` is closed under multiplication:
a product of two such products is again one. -/
theorem mul_mem_span_productSet {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (c : C ⟶ A)
    (d : D ⟶ A) {V : SmallEtale B S hS F} {y₁ y₂ : A.right.obj.obj (op V)}
    (h₁ : y₁ ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (productSet c d V))
    (h₂ : y₂ ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (productSet c d V)) :
    y₁ * y₂ ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (productSet c d V) := by
  refine mul_mem_span_of_forall_mul_mem h₁ h₂ fun p hp q hq => ?_
  obtain ⟨x, x', rfl⟩ := hp
  obtain ⟨y, y', rfl⟩ := hq
  refine Submodule.subset_span ⟨x * y, x' * y', ?_⟩
  simp only [map_mul]
  ring

/-! ### Products of sections over a smaller affine chart -/

/-- The image under a morphism of algebra sheaves of a section over the smaller of two affine
étale charts lies in the span of the restrictions of the images of the sections over the larger
one, as soon as the source is cartesian on affine charts. -/
theorem mem_span_range_app_restrict {A C : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (f : C ⟶ A)
    {W V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (g : V ⟶ W)
    (hC : Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange C.underlyingModule g))
    (x : C.right.obj.obj (op V)) :
    f.right.hom.app (op V) x ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      (Set.range fun t : C.right.obj.obj (op W) =>
        A.right.obj.map g.op (f.right.hom.app (op W) t)) := by
  have hx : x ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      (Set.range fun t : C.right.obj.obj (op W) => C.right.obj.map g.op t) :=
    mem_span_range_chartRestrict C.underlyingModule g hC x
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
      obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hy
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨t, (app_map f g.op t).symm⟩
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add y₁ y₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ h₁ h₂
  | smul r y _ h =>
      rw [show f.right.hom.app (op V) (r • y) = r • f.right.hom.app (op V) y from
        app_mul_algebraMap f (op V) r y]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r h

/-- **Every product of sections over the smaller of two affine étale charts lies in the span of
the restrictions of the products of sections over the larger one**, provided `C` and `D` are
cartesian on affine charts.

Cartesianness writes a section over the smaller chart as a combination of restrictions, and
multiplication of sections is bilinear for the chart ring, so a product of two such combinations
is a combination of restrictions of products. -/
theorem productSet_restrict_subset_span {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF}
    (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A)
    (hC : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts C.underlyingModule)
    (hD : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts D.underlyingModule)
    {W V : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hW : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V))
    (g : V ⟶ W) :
    productSet c d V ⊆ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      ((fun y => A.right.obj.map g.op y) '' productSet c d W) := by
  rintro y ⟨x, x', rfl⟩
  exact mul_mem_span_of_forall_mul_mem
    (mem_span_range_app_restrict c g (hC W V hW hV g).2 x)
    (mem_span_range_app_restrict d g (hD W V hW hV g).2 x') (by
      rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩ _ ⟨t', rfl⟩
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, ⟨t, t', rfl⟩, by simp only [map_mul]⟩)

/-! ### Descent of membership in the span of the products -/

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_of_forall_restrict_mem_span` for the sections of an algebra
sheaf: a section over an affine étale chart lies in the span of a finite family of sections as
soon as its restriction to each member of a jointly faithfully flat finite family of affine
charts lies in the span of the restricted family. -/
theorem mem_span_range_of_forall_restrict (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    (hA : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts A.underlyingModule) {W : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hW : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
    {n : ℕ} {z : Fin n → SmallEtale B S hS F} (φ : ∀ i, z i ⟶ W)
    (hz : ∀ i, IsAffine
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (z i)))
    (hff : (RingHom.pi fun i => chartRestrict (hF := hF) (φ i)).FaithfullyFlat)
    {κ : Type u} [Finite κ] (τ : κ → A.right.obj.obj (op W))
    {a : A.right.obj.obj (op W)}
    (hx : ∀ i, A.right.obj.map (φ i).op a ∈
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF (z i))
        (Set.range fun l => A.right.obj.map (φ i).op (τ l))) :
    a ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF W) (Set.range τ) :=
  mem_span_of_forall_restrict_mem_span A.underlyingModule hA hW φ hz hff τ hx

/-- **A single finite family of products of sections of `C` and `D` over an affine étale chart
whose restrictions span the restrictions of a given section to every member of a finite family
of affine charts.**

Each member contributes a finite family by `Submodule.mem_span_finite_of_mem_span` applied to
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.productSet_restrict_subset_span`, and the sigma type of
those finitely many finite families is a single finite family. -/
theorem exists_finite_productSet_of_forall_restrict
    {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A)
    (hC : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts C.underlyingModule)
    (hD : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts D.underlyingModule)
    {W : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hW : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
    {n : ℕ} {z : Fin n → SmallEtale B S hS F} (φ : ∀ i, z i ⟶ W)
    (hz : ∀ i, IsAffine
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (z i)))
    {a : A.right.obj.obj (op W)}
    (ha : ∀ i, A.right.obj.map (φ i).op a ∈
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF (z i)) (productSet c d (z i))) :
    ∃ (κ : Type u) (_ : Finite κ) (τ : κ → A.right.obj.obj (op W)),
      (∀ l, τ l ∈ productSet c d W) ∧
        ∀ i, A.right.obj.map (φ i).op a ∈
          Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF (z i))
            (Set.range fun l => A.right.obj.map (φ i).op (τ l)) := by
  have ha' : ∀ i, A.right.obj.map (φ i).op a ∈
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF (z i))
        ((fun y => A.right.obj.map (φ i).op y) '' productSet c d W) := fun i =>
    Submodule.span_le.2
      (productSet_restrict_subset_span c d hC hD hW (hz i) (φ i)) (ha i)
  choose T hTsub hTmem using fun i => Submodule.mem_span_finite_of_mem_span (ha' i)
  have hpre : ∀ (i : Fin n) (l : {y // y ∈ T i}), ∃ v ∈ productSet c d W,
      A.right.obj.map (φ i).op v = (l : A.right.obj.obj (op (z i))) := fun i l => hTsub i l.2
  choose v hv hvl using hpre
  refine ⟨Σ j : Fin n, {y // y ∈ T j}, inferInstance, fun l => v l.1 l.2,
    fun l => hv l.1 l.2, fun i => ?_⟩
  refine Submodule.span_mono ?_ (hTmem i)
  intro y hy
  exact ⟨⟨i, ⟨y, hy⟩⟩, hvl i ⟨y, hy⟩⟩

/-- **A section of `A` over an affine étale chart lies in the `𝒪_F`-span of the products of
sections of `C` and `D` as soon as its restriction to each member of a finite jointly faithfully
flat family of affine étale charts does.**

The finite family of products supplied by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.exists_finite_productSet_of_forall_restrict` is descended
by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_of_forall_restrict_mem_span`. -/
theorem mem_span_productSet_of_forall_restrict
    {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A)
    (hA : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts A.underlyingModule)
    (hC : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts C.underlyingModule)
    (hD : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts D.underlyingModule)
    {W : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hW : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
    {n : ℕ} {z : Fin n → SmallEtale B S hS F} (φ : ∀ i, z i ⟶ W)
    (hz : ∀ i, IsAffine
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (z i)))
    (hff : (RingHom.pi fun i => chartRestrict (hF := hF) (φ i)).FaithfullyFlat)
    {a : A.right.obj.obj (op W)}
    (ha : ∀ i, A.right.obj.map (φ i).op a ∈
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF (z i)) (productSet c d (z i))) :
    a ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF W) (productSet c d W) := by
  obtain ⟨κ, _, τ, hτ, hx⟩ :=
    exists_finite_productSet_of_forall_restrict c d hC hD hW φ hz ha
  refine Submodule.span_mono ?_
    (mem_span_range_of_forall_restrict A hA hW φ hz hff τ hx)
  rintro y ⟨l, rfl⟩
  exact hτ l

/-! ### The span of the products is the generated subring -/

/-- **The `𝒪_F(V)`-span of the products of sections of `C` and `D` is the subring of `A(V)`
generated by the images of `C(V)` and of `D(V)`.**

The generated subring is stable under the scalar action because the structure-algebra map of `A`
factors through `c`, and the span is a subring because the products are closed under
multiplication and contain `1`. -/
theorem span_productSet_eq_closure {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF}
    (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (V : SmallEtale B S hS F) :
    (Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (productSet c d V) :
        Set (A.right.obj.obj (op V))) =
      (Subring.closure (Set.range (fun x : C.right.obj.obj (op V) =>
            c.right.hom.app (op V) x) ∪
          Set.range fun x : D.right.obj.obj (op V) => d.right.hom.app (op V) x) :
        Set (A.right.obj.obj (op V))) := by
  have hcmem : ∀ x : C.right.obj.obj (op V), c.right.hom.app (op V) x ∈
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (productSet c d V) := fun x =>
    Submodule.subset_span ⟨x, 1, by rw [map_one, mul_one]⟩
  have hdmem : ∀ x : D.right.obj.obj (op V), d.right.hom.app (op V) x ∈
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (productSet c d V) := fun x =>
    Submodule.subset_span ⟨1, x, by rw [map_one, one_mul]⟩
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm (fun y hy => ?_) (fun y hy => ?_)
  · rw [SetLike.mem_coe] at hy ⊢
    induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem w hw =>
        obtain ⟨x, x', rfl⟩ := hw
        exact mul_mem (Subring.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨x, rfl⟩))
          (Subring.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨x', rfl⟩))
    | zero => exact zero_mem _
    | add w₁ w₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ => exact add_mem h₁ h₂
    | smul r w _ h =>
        exact mul_mem (Subring.subset_closure
          (Or.inl ⟨C.algebraMap (op V) r, c.comm (op V) r⟩)) h
  · rw [SetLike.mem_coe] at hy ⊢
    induction hy using Subring.closure_induction with
    | mem w hw =>
        rcases hw with ⟨x, rfl⟩ | ⟨x, rfl⟩
        · exact hcmem x
        · exact hdmem x
    | zero => exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | one => exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨1, 1, by rw [map_one, map_one, one_mul]⟩
    | add w₁ w₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ => exact Submodule.add_mem _ h₁ h₂
    | neg w _ h => exact Submodule.neg_mem _ h
    | mul w₁ w₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ => exact mul_mem_span_productSet c d h₁ h₂

/-! ### The descent under quasi-coherence -/

/-- **A section of a quasi-coherent algebra sheaf over an affine étale chart lies in the span of
the products of sections of two quasi-coherent algebras mapping to it as soon as its restriction
to each member of a finite jointly faithfully flat family of affine charts does.**

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.mem_span_productSet_of_forall_restrict` with
cartesianness on affine charts supplied by Descent, Proposition 03DX(2). -/
theorem mem_span_productSet_of_forall_restrict_of_isQuasicoherent
    {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A)
    (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent) (hC : C.IsQuasicoherent) (hD : D.IsQuasicoherent)
    {W : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hW : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
    {n : ℕ} {z : Fin n → SmallEtale B S hS F} (φ : ∀ i, z i ⟶ W)
    (hz : ∀ i, IsAffine
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (z i)))
    (hff : (RingHom.pi fun i => chartRestrict (hF := hF) (φ i)).FaithfullyFlat)
    {a : A.right.obj.obj (op W)}
    (ha : ∀ i, A.right.obj.map (φ i).op a ∈
      Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF (z i)) (productSet c d (z i))) :
    a ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF W) (productSet c d W) :=
  mem_span_productSet_of_forall_restrict c d
